T-D06 / CT-006 contract for the golden_window fixture (window 2026-07-01..
2026-07-31, as_of=2026-07-31, window_days=30):

  Per-type reopen block (CT-006 field shape: reopened, closed, window,
  dedup_rows_removed, rate):

    Bug:     { "reopened": 1, "closed": 5, "rate": 0.2 }
    Task:    { "reopened": 0, "closed": 2, "rate": 0.0 }
    Feature: { "reopened": 0, "closed": 1, "rate": 0.0 }

  Overall (aggregated across all three types):

    { "reopened": 1, "closed": 8, "rate": 0.125 }

  "excluded_retroactive": [] -- this fixture deliberately contains no
  Opened->closure created_at gap under 60 seconds (see
  negative_control_retroactive/ for that mechanic in isolation).

HAND-COMPUTED GROUND TRUTH (independent of any reopen_rate.py invocation --
this is the derivation the RED test's own Python cross-check performs and
compares byte-for-byte against, per §11.4.245's DERIVED-oracle strategy):

  Bug population = 6 items (B-001..B-006). B-005's ONLY closure event
  (Fixed on_date=2026-06-20) falls BEFORE window.from=2026-07-01, so B-005
  is NOT a member of closed_in_window -- 5 Bug items remain
  (B-001,B-002,B-003,B-004,B-006). Of those 5, B-001 has a Reopened event
  on_date=2026-07-10 (inside the window) -- it is the only Bug member whose
  Reopened event ALSO falls inside the window. B-006 DOES carry a Reopened
  event, but its on_date=2026-08-05 is AFTER window.to=2026-07-31, so B-006
  contributes to the DENOMINATOR (closed=5) but NOT the numerator
  (reopened stays 1, not 2) -- this is the numerator/denominator window
  boundary distinguished from B-005's pure denominator boundary.
  Bug: reopened=1, closed=5, rate = 1/5 = 0.2 exactly.

  Task population = 2 items (T-001, T-002), both Completed inside the
  window, neither reopened. Task: reopened=0, closed=2, rate = 0/2 = 0.0.

  Feature population = 1 item (F-001), Implemented inside the window, not
  reopened. Feature: reopened=0, closed=1, rate = 0/1 = 0.0.

  Overall: closed = 5 + 2 + 1 = 8; reopened = 1 + 0 + 0 = 1;
  rate = 1/8 = 0.125 exactly.

MUST NOT appear anywhere in the output for this fixture: B-005 counted
toward any type's closed population; B-006's Reopened event counted toward
the numerator; any rate computed over a DIFFERENT population than the one
named above (e.g. a naive whole-history count instead of the windowed,
matched population -- this is exactly the class golden_bad_mismatched_
populations/ tests as a rejection case; here it must simply be CORRECT);
"RATE_NOT_COMPUTABLE" anywhere (this fixture's populations are clean and
matched, so a real numeric rate is the only correct answer for every type
and overall).

Paired-mutation targets this fixture protects against (T093): counting a
Reopened event outside the window toward the numerator (would inflate Bug
to reopened=2, rate=0.4); counting a closure event outside the window
toward the denominator (would inflate Bug to closed=6); computing the
overall rate as an average-of-per-type-rates instead of a
sum-of-counts ratio (0.2+0+0)/3 = 0.0667 would silently disagree with the
correct 0.125 -- the exact-match assertion below catches either defect the
instant it is introduced.
